# Feature — Search Transaction

## Overview
Full-text search across all transactions by amount, notes, and category.
Accessed via search icon on Home AppBar or History AppBar.

## No new data layer needed
Search reuses existing `TransactionRepository` and `transaction_provider.dart`.
Add a `searchTransactions(String query)` method to the existing repository.

## Update Existing Repository
```dart
// Add to transaction_repository.dart (abstract)
Future<List<Transaction>> searchTransactions(String query);

// Add to transaction_repository_impl.dart
Future<List<Transaction>> searchTransactions(String query) async {
  final all = await datasource.getAllTransactions();
  final q = query.toLowerCase();
  return all.where((tx) {
    final category = kCategories.firstWhere((c) => c.id == tx.categoryId);
    return category.label.toLowerCase().contains(q) ||
           (tx.notes?.toLowerCase().contains(q) ?? false) ||
           formatRupiah(tx.amount).contains(q);
  }).toList();
}
```

## Search Provider
```dart
// Add to transaction_provider.dart
final searchQueryProvider = StateProvider<String>((ref) => '');

final searchResultsProvider = Provider<List<Transaction>>((ref) {
  final query = ref.watch(searchQueryProvider);
  final all = ref.watch(allTransactionsProvider).value ?? [];
  if (query.isEmpty) return [];
  final q = query.toLowerCase();
  return all.where((tx) {
    final category = kCategories.firstWhere((c) => c.id == tx.categoryId);
    return category.label.toLowerCase().contains(q) ||
           (tx.notes?.toLowerCase().contains(q) ?? false) ||
           formatRupiah(tx.amount).contains(q);
  }).toList();
});
```

## Screen Specification — search_page.dart
- Full screen pushed page (not a tab)
- iOS-style search bar at top (autofocus on open)
- Search bar: rounded, gray background (#F5F5F5), black text
- Clear button (✕) appears when text is not empty
- Results: ListView using TransactionItem widget
- Empty state (no query): show "Search by category, notes, or amount"
- Empty state (no results): show "No results for '[query]'"
- Real-time search — filter on every keystroke (debounce 300ms)
- Each result shows: category icon, label, date, amount, notes preview

## Widget — search_bar_widget.dart
```dart
